## 1. Executive Summary

A critical-severity condition was identified and requires immediate manual validation. We enumerated **0 subdomains** of **app.example.com** and identified **0 externally reachable services**, recording **5 observations** (1 high, 2 medium, 2 low/info). The broader pattern is **inconsistent edge hardening** — chiefly legacy TLS and HTTP security-header configuration applied unevenly across hosts. Most individual observations do not independently represent a material compromise path and are best addressed as platform/edge configuration issues rather than application-by-application vulnerabilities (see Root issues). A small number of observations warrant immediate manual validation — see the High-severity items, each carrying an explicit confidence and validation state. Exploitation, authenticated testing, and destructive checks were out of scope; findings marked *version-inferred* or *config-inferred* are leads pending validation, not confirmed vulnerabilities.

