## 2. Methodology

Testing followed a phased, non-destructive external methodology aligned to OWASP WSTG:

1. **Passive reconnaissance** — subdomain enumeration (subfinder), certificate-transparency, and OSINT (Shodan: IP space, ASN/org, open ports, product/version, TXT/SaaS).
2. **Resolution & live-host discovery** — DNS resolution (dnsx) then HTTP/S probing (httpx) of resolved hosts only.
3. **Active testing (rate-limited, in-scope)** — security headers, TLS version posture, unauthenticated-exposure paths (baseline-differential to avoid catch-all false positives), and component-version CVE lookup via OSV.
4. **Classification & direction** — every finding mapped to an OWASP category (Web/Mobile/LLM), CWE, and an OWASP Cheat Sheet, with per-stack remediation recipes.

Destructive, credential, and deep (nuclei/cipher-enumeration) tests were **out of scope** for this pass and are recommended as an authorized follow-up (see §8).

