  <p class="note">Compliance control references are provided to assist audit evidence collection (e.g., SOC 2). They indicate the criteria a finding is relevant to; they are not a statement of audit opinion.</p></section><section class="page"><h2>1. Executive Summary</h2><p>A critical-severity condition was identified requiring immediate manual validation. We enumerated 0 subdomains of app.example.com and identified 0 externally reachable services, recording 5 observations (1 high, 2 medium, 2 low/info). The broader pattern is inconsistent edge hardening — chiefly legacy TLS and HTTP security-header configuration applied unevenly. Most individual observations do not independently represent a material compromise path and are best addressed as platform/edge configuration issues (see Root issues) rather than application-by-application vulnerabilities. A small number warrant immediate manual validation. Findings carry explicit Confidence and Validation states; those marked version-inferred or config-inferred are leads pending validation, not confirmed vulnerabilities. Exploitation and authenticated testing were out of scope.</p>
  <h3>Risk profile</h3><div class="heat">
  <div class="heat-cell sev-critical"><div class="hc-n">1</div><div class="hc-l">CRITICAL</div></div><div class="heat-cell sev-high"><div class="hc-n">0</div><div class="hc-l">HIGH</div></div><div class="heat-cell sev-medium"><div class="hc-n">2</div><div class="hc-l">MEDIUM</div></div><div class="heat-cell sev-low"><div class="hc-n">1</div><div class="hc-l">LOW</div></div><div class="heat-cell sev-informational"><div class="hc-n">1</div><div class="hc-l">INFORMATIONAL</div></div>
  <div class="heat-cell total"><div class="hc-n">5</div><div class="hc-l">OBSERVATIONS</div></div></div>
  <h3>Root issues (observations collapsed)</h3><div class="rem"><table class="grid"><tbody><tr><td>Root issue</td><td>Highest severity</td><td>Affected (applicable)</td><td>Non-applicable/suppressed</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>CRITICAL</td><td>2</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Deprecated TLS/cipher support (edge TLS policy)</td><td>MEDIUM</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Missing/weak Content-Security-Policy (edge header policy)</td><td>LOW</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table><p>**5 observations collapse to 3 root issues.** Repeated control failures on many hosts are one platform/edge issue, not many independent vulnerabilities.</p></div>
  <h3>Key findings</h3><ul class="keys">
  <li><span class="pill sev-critical">CRITICAL</span> SQL injection in search parameter <span class="host">https://app.example.com/search?q=</span></li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Assessment coverage</h3><table class="grid"><tbody>
  <tr><td>Subdomains enumerated</td><td>0</td></tr>
