  </tbody></table></section><section class="page"><h2>4. Root Findings</h2>
  <p>Observations are collapsed to root findings (one per control per asset-group). Per-observation detail and evidence ids are in the Observation Detail appendix.</p>
  <div class="finding">
    <div class="f-head"><span class="fid">R-001</span><span class="pill sev-critical">CRITICAL</span><h3>SQL injection in search parameter</h3></div>
    <table class="grid f-meta"><tbody>
    <tr><td>Affected endpoints</td><td>2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Confidence / Validation / State</td><td>Confirmed / passive / OBSERVED</td></tr>
    <tr><td>OWASP / CWE</td><td>A03:2021 Injection / CWE-79</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Detector</td><td><code>generic@1</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Control (detector)</td><td><code>generic@1</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>CVSS v3.1</td><td><code>CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H = 9.8</code></td></tr>
    
    
    
    <tr><td>Remediation SLA</td><td>7 days</td></tr>
    <tr><td>SOC 2 / ISO / PCI</td><td>CC7.1, CC8.1 (secure SDLC) / A.8.28 secure coding, A.8.26 application security requirements / 6.2.4 (injection defenses), 6.3</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Owning team</td><td>Application teams / AppSec</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="f-body"><p><b>Affected endpoints.</b> https://app.example.com/search?q=, https://app.example.com/</p>
    <p><b>Business risk.</b> An attacker could run unintended queries or code, leading to data theft or service compromise.</p>
    <p><b>Severity rationale.</b> <p>CVSS base 9.8 (CRITICAL band), consistent with the assessment severity.</p></p>
    <p><b>Technical impact.</b> Untrusted input reaching an interpreter enables data theft, code execution, or client-side compromise.</p>
    
    <p><b>Remediation.</b></p><div class="rem"><p>1. **Parameterized queries / prepared statements.** Never concatenate input into SQL.</p><p>2. **Stored procedures** (when they do not build dynamic SQL internally).</p><p>3. **Allow-list input validation** for identifiers that cannot be parameterized (table/column names).</p><p>4. **Escaping** only as a last resort, DB-specific.</p><p>5. Least-privilege DB account; disable multi-statements.</p><p>Example — safe (parameterized):</p><p><code></code>`sql</p><p>-- BAD:  &#34;SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = &#34; + id</p><p>-- GOOD:</p><p>SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?      -- bind id as a parameter</p><p><code></code>`</p><ul><li>**Context-aware output encoding** at the sink: HTML body, HTML attribute, JS,</li></ul><p>CSS, and URL contexts each need their own encoding.</p><ul><li>Prefer a framework&#39;s auto-escaping template; avoid <code>innerHTML</code>,</li></ul><p><code>dangerouslySetInnerHTML</code>, <code>document.write</code>, <code>v-html</code>.</p><ul><li>**DOM XSS:** use safe sinks (<code>textContent</code>, <code>setAttribute</code>); treat</li></ul><p><code>location</code>, <code>document.referrer</code>, <code>window.name</code>, <code>postMessage</code> data as untrusted.</p></div>
    </div></div><div class="finding">
    <div class="f-head"><span class="fid">R-002</span><span class="pill sev-medium">MEDIUM</span><h3>Unauthenticated sensitive path</h3></div>
    <table class="grid f-meta"><tbody>
    <tr><td>Affected endpoints</td><td>1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Confidence / Validation / State</td><td>Confirmed / behavior-confirmed / CONFIRMED</td></tr>
    <tr><td>OWASP / CWE</td><td>A05:2021 Security Misconfiguration / CWE-527</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Detector</td><td><code>http.exposure-path@1</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Control (detector)</td><td><code>http.exposure-path@1</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>CVSS v3.1</td><td><code>CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N = 5.3</code></td></tr>
    
    
    
    <tr><td>Remediation SLA</td><td>90 days</td></tr>
    <tr><td>SOC 2 / ISO / PCI</td><td>CC6.1 (logical access), CC6.6 (perimeter), CC7.2 (monitoring) / A.8.20 network security, A.8.9 config management / 1.2/1.3 (network), 2.2 (secure config), 6.4.1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Owning team</td><td>Platform / Edge / SRE</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="f-body"><p><b>Affected endpoints.</b> https://app.example.com/.git/HEAD</p>
    <p><b>Business risk.</b> Operational internals are exposed to anyone on the internet, aiding a targeted attack and potentially leaking secrets.</p>
    <p><b>Severity rationale.</b> <p>CVSS base 5.3 (MEDIUM band), consistent with the assessment severity.</p></p>
    <p><b>Technical impact.</b> Missing hardening or exposed operational endpoints disclose internal state and enable clickjacking, MIME-sniffing, or cross-origin abuse; exposed metrics/config can leak topology, versions, and secrets.</p>
    
    <p><b>Remediation.</b></p><div class="rem"><ul><li>Restrict or remove the exposed endpoint; require authentication.</li><li>If it is a debug/config/VCS artifact, disable it in production and rotate any exposed secrets.</li></ul></div>
    </div></div><div class="finding">
    <div class="f-head"><span class="fid">R-003</span><span class="pill sev-medium">MEDIUM</span><h3>Deprecated TLS / weak cipher policy</h3></div>
    <table class="grid f-meta"><tbody>
    <tr><td>Affected endpoints</td><td>1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Confidence / Validation / State</td><td>Confirmed / behavior-confirmed / CONFIRMED</td></tr>
    <tr><td>OWASP / CWE</td><td>A02:2021 Cryptographic Failures / CWE-326</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Detector</td><td><code>tls.deprecated-protocol@1</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Control (detector)</td><td><code>tls.deprecated-protocol@1</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>CVSS v3.1</td><td><code>CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N = 4.8</code></td></tr>
    
    
    
    <tr><td>Remediation SLA</td><td>90 days</td></tr>
    <tr><td>SOC 2 / ISO / PCI</td><td>CC6.1, CC6.7 (transmission of data) / A.8.24 cryptography, A.5.33 protection of records / 4.1/4.2 (strong cryptography in transit)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Owning team</td><td>Platform / Edge</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="f-body"><p><b>Affected endpoints.</b> app.example.com:443</p>
    <p><b>Business risk.</b> On a hostile network, an on-path attacker with a suitable client/cipher/downgrade condition could intercept sessions to this host. Requires network position — not remotely exploitable by itself.</p>
    <p><b>Severity rationale.</b> <p>CVSS base 4.8 (MEDIUM band), consistent with the assessment severity.</p></p>
    <p><b>Technical impact.</b> Deprecated TLS and missing HSTS enable downgrade/MITM and session interception on hostile networks.</p>
    
    <p><b>Remediation.</b></p><div class="rem"><ul><li>Disable TLS 1.0 and TLS 1.1; require TLS 1.2+ (prefer TLS 1.3).</li><li>Remove obsolete cipher suites (3DES, RC4, EXPORT, NULL, static-DH).</li><li>Enforce the policy centrally at the load balancer / ingress / CDN.</li><li>Validate client compatibility, then retest protocol negotiation.</li></ul></div>
    </div></div><div class="finding">
    <div class="f-head"><span class="fid">R-004</span><span class="pill sev-low">LOW</span><h3>Missing Content-Security-Policy</h3></div>
    <table class="grid f-meta"><tbody>
    <tr><td>Affected endpoints</td><td>1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Confidence / Validation / State</td><td>Confirmed / passive / OBSERVED</td></tr>
    <tr><td>OWASP / CWE</td><td>A05:2021 Security Misconfiguration / CWE-1021</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Detector</td><td><code>http.header.csp-missing@1</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Control (detector)</td><td><code>http.header.csp-missing@1</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>CVSS v3.1</td><td><code>CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N = 5.3</code></td></tr>
    
    
    
    <tr><td>Remediation SLA</td><td>next release</td></tr>
    <tr><td>SOC 2 / ISO / PCI</td><td>CC6.1 (logical access), CC6.6 (perimeter), CC7.2 (monitoring) / A.8.20 network security, A.8.9 config management / 1.2/1.3 (network), 2.2 (secure config), 6.4.1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Owning team</td><td>Platform / Edge / SRE</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <div class="f-body"><p><b>Affected endpoints.</b> https://app.example.com/</p>
    <p><b>Business risk.</b> Limited standalone risk. No XSS was demonstrated; without CSP, an XSS elsewhere in the app would not be contained.</p>
    <p><b>Severity rationale.</b> <p>CVSS base score 5.3 (MEDIUM band); **assessment severity LOW** — no demonstrated exploit prerequisite; defense-in-depth only.</p></p>
    <p><b>Technical impact.</b> Missing hardening or exposed operational endpoints disclose internal state and enable clickjacking, MIME-sniffing, or cross-origin abuse; exposed metrics/config can leak topology, versions, and secrets.</p>
    
    <p><b>Remediation.</b></p><div class="rem"><ul><li>Add a restrictive <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> (nonce/hash for inline; <code>object-src &amp;#39;none&amp;#39;</code>, <code>base-uri &amp;#39;none&amp;#39;</code>).</li><li>Only material for HTML responses; scope the policy to rendered pages.</li><li>Roll out in <code>Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only</code> first, then enforce.</li></ul></div>
    </div></div>
  <h3>Observation Detail</h3><div class="rem"><table class="grid"><tbody><tr><td>Obs key</td><td>Asset</td><td>Severity</td><td>State</td><td>Detector</td><td>Evidence</td><td>Observed at</td></tr><tr><td><code>cea32e2e06476082</code></td><td>https://app.example.com/search?q=</td><td>CRITICAL</td><td>OBSERVED</td><td><code>generic@1</code></td><td><code>—</code></td><td><TIME></td></tr><tr><td><code>a621edae6c631a50</code></td><td>https://app.example.com/.git/HEAD</td><td>MEDIUM</td><td>CONFIRMED</td><td><code>http.exposure-path@1</code></td><td><code>—</code></td><td><TIME></td></tr><tr><td><code>29442c004311e380</code></td><td>app.example.com:443</td><td>MEDIUM</td><td>CONFIRMED</td><td><code>tls.deprecated-protocol@1</code></td><td><code>—</code></td><td><TIME></td></tr><tr><td><code>1a8bb2e905196640</code></td><td>https://app.example.com/</td><td>LOW</td><td>OBSERVED</td><td><code>http.header.csp-missing@1</code></td><td><code>—</code></td><td><TIME></td></tr><tr><td><code>cea32e2e06476082</code></td><td>https://app.example.com/</td><td>INFORMATIONAL</td><td>OBSERVED</td><td><code>generic@1</code></td><td><code>—</code></td><td><TIME></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="page"><h2>5. Attack Narrative</h2><p>During reconnaissance, 0 subdomains were enumerated and 0 live services identified. Highest-impact observations: SQL injection in search parameter (https://app.example.com/search?q=). Chaining the observed conditions (confidence preserved):

- **[confirmed disclosure]** an unauthenticated operational endpoint returned internal detail (see the finding&#39;s Observed Evidence) → improves target selection and topology/version intelligence
- **[requires network position]** deprecated TLS 1.0/1.1 acceptance → interception is possible only for an on-path attacker with a vulnerable client/cipher/downgrade condition, not remotely by itself

No edge in this chain reaches a demonstrated compromise: the confirmed links are information-disclosure and configuration, and the exploit link is an unvalidated hypothesis. A credentialed follow-up would be required to extend this into authenticated authorization and business-logic testing.</p>
  <h3>Attack-path exploration</h3><div class="rem"><p>**Aggression profile:** safe-active</p><p>The engine explored **2 candidate attack path(s)**, advanced **1** beyond initial discovery, and validated **0** intermediate primitive(s). No path reached the defined impact boundary (no state change, no data exfiltration, no credential use).</p><table class="grid"><tbody><tr><td>Attack path</td><td>Opened by</td><td>Advanced</td><td>Validated</td><td>Termination reason</td></tr><tr><td>Anonymous-read data exposure</td><td><code>anonymous_read</code></td><td>yes</td><td>—</td><td><code>STOP_POLICY_BOUNDARY</code></td></tr><tr><td>Internal-topology reconnaissance</td><td><code>reveals_internal_hostnames</code></td><td>—</td><td>—</td><td><code>STOP_NO_REACHABLE_TARGET</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>**Termination reasons** (why each path stopped — distinguishes &#34;controls resisted&#34; from &#34;scanner could not continue&#34;):</p><ul><li><code>STOP_NO_REACHABLE_TARGET</code>: 1</li><li><code>STOP_POLICY_BOUNDARY</code>: 1</li></ul><p>_Paths are derived from the capabilities each finding grants (capability model), not from prose. A path &#34;advances&#34; when a second capability extends it and &#34;validates&#34; when a harmless primitive (OAST callback, redirect-to-canary, arithmetic SSTI) confirms an intermediate step._</p></div>
