  <h3>Attack-graph metrics</h3><div class="rem"><table class="grid"><tbody><tr><td>Metric</td><td>Value</td></tr><tr><td>Planner attack-graph edges</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Maximum attack-graph depth</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Capability types produced</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Capability types consumed by planner</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Dead capabilities (produced, never pivoted)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>Branches blocked by engagement policy</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Proof boundaries reached (validated, then stopped)</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table><p>_Depth/branch metrics measure adversarial *reasoning*, not probe volume: a high edge count with depth 1 is broad-but-shallow; depth &gt;1 means a discovery chained into further decisions. Policy-blocked branches are where the engine could have continued but the adversarial-readonly boundary stopped it._</p></div>
