  <p>Raw data (subdomains, live services, findings JSON, Shodan OSINT, nuclei output) accompanies this report in <code>data/</code> for team distribution and re-testing (<code>secskills report --retest app.example.com</code>). Ticket export: <code>secskills tickets app.example.com</code>.</p></section><section class="page"><h2>Appendix B — Tools &amp; Cleanup Log</h2><div class="rem"><p>### Tools used</p><ul><li>osv-scanner (OSV API)</li><li>secskills native check engine</li></ul><p>### Cleanup log (test-artifact attestation)</p><p>This was a **non-destructive** assessment. secskills sends only GET/HEAD/OPTIONS and read-only requests; it does **not** create accounts, upload files, plant web shells, or write to the target. Therefore:</p><ul><li>Test accounts created: **none**</li><li>Web shells / payloads planted: **none**</li><li>Data written to target: **none**</li><li>Credentials used: **none** (unauthenticated assessment)</li></ul><p>No cleanup actions are required on the target.</p></div></section><section class="page"><h2>Root-Cause Clustering (shared configuration)</h2><div class="rem"><p>### Deprecated TLS / weak cipher policy (edge)</p><p>1 observations across 1 shared-configuration group(s):</p><ul><li>**G1 — 1 asset(s)** (no shared-infra signal (grouped as unclustered)): app.example.com</li></ul><p>### Missing security-header policy (edge)</p><p>1 observations across 1 shared-configuration group(s):</p><ul><li>**G1 — 1 asset(s)** (no shared-infra signal (grouped as unclustered)): app.example.com</li></ul><p>### Unauthenticated operational exposure</p><p>1 observations across 1 shared-configuration group(s):</p><ul><li>**G1 — 1 asset(s)** (no shared-infra signal (grouped as unclustered)): app.example.com</li></ul><p>_Grouping is by shared-infrastructure signature (resolved /24 + web server + CNAME suffix). Remediating the shared ingress/config fixes every asset in a group at once._</p></div></section><section class="page"><h2>Detector Quality Scorecard</h2><div class="rem"><table class="grid"><tbody><tr><td>Detector family</td><td>TP</td><td>FP</td><td>FN</td><td>Precision</td><td>Recall</td></tr><tr><td><code>component.banner-osv-correlation@1</code></td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>http.cors@1</code></td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>http.exposure-path@1</code></td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>http.header.csp-missing@1</code></td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>http.header.hsts-missing@1</code></td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>http.header.nosniff-missing@1</code></td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>http.prometheus.public-metrics@1</code></td><td>4</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>llm.canary-reflection@1</code></td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>llm.response-drift@1</code></td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>llm.system-prompt-leak@1</code></td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><code>tls.deprecated-protocol@1</code></td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>100%</td><td>100%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>_Measured against the committed offline regression corpus (<code>secskills conformance</code>). Every fixed report inconsistency adds a fixture, so it cannot regress silently._</p></div></section><section class="page"><h2>Evidence Object Index</h2><div class="rem"><p>_No immutable evidence objects were captured for this run._</p></div></section><section class="page"><h2>Severity Rubric (independent of CVSS)</h2><div class="rem"><p>**HIGH** — at least one of: confirmed sensitive-data disclosure; confirmed unauthorized state-changing action; a validated, remotely-reachable exploit primitive; or a material authentication/authorization weakness.</p><p>**MEDIUM** — a confirmed weakness that is exploitable only with a precondition (network position, a second flaw, specific client), or unauthenticated exposure of non-sensitive operational data.</p><p>**LOW** — a defense-in-depth / hardening deviation with no demonstrated exploit prerequisite.</p><p>**INFORMATIONAL** — an observation with no security weakness; context only.</p><p>CVSS base score is computed separately (FIRST.org). Where the rubric severity differs from the CVSS band, the finding states the reason; the rubric governs the assessment severity.</p><p>**Severity is impact-if-true and does NOT imply validation.** A finding&#39;s <code>State</code> (CONFIRMED / OBSERVED / INFERRED / INCONCLUSIVE) carries the validation status. A MEDIUM/INCONCLUSIVE finding means &#34;medium impact IF the condition holds; not confirmed this run&#34; — it is not a confirmed medium weakness.</p></div></section><section class="page"><h2>Control Test Ledger</h2><div class="rem"><table class="grid"><tbody><tr><td>Control family</td><td>Eligible</td><td>Tested</td><td>Passed</td><td>Failed</td><td>Inconclusive</td><td>N/A</td></tr><tr><td>cors</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>security-headers</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>tls-version</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>unauth-exposure</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>**Total**</td><td>**0**</td><td>**0**</td><td>**0**</td><td>**0**</td><td>**0**</td><td>**0**</td></tr></tbody></table><p>_Denominator semantics: **Eligible** = control applies to the endpoint (TLS-version applies only to HTTPS; HTTP-only endpoints are **N/A**). **Tested** = eligible endpoints reachable at test time (Tested = Passed + Failed). **Inconclusive** = eligible but unreachable/errored — never counted as Passed/secure. Eligible = Tested + Inconclusive._</p></div></section><section class="page"><h2>Run Attestation</h2><div class="rem"><p>_Run attestation not available._</p></div></section><footer class="doc-foot">secskills v0.32.1 — Confidential — generated <TODAY> — Report SHA-256 <SHA256></footer></body></html>
